osl-ephys is developed by the OHBA Methods Group at the University of Oxford
(https://www.psych.ox.ac.uk/research/ohba-analysis-group).

Core developers
  Chetan Gohil
  Andrew J. Quinn
  Mats W. J. van Es
  Mark W. Woolrich

Contributors
  SungJun Cho (sign flipping solvers)
  Richard Csaky
  Marco Fabus
  Miguel Farinha
  Hongyu Qian
  Harrison Ritz
  Rob Seymour (OPM support)
  Jize Zhang (simultaneous EEG-fMRI preprocessing, osl-pathfinder)

The sign flipping solvers come from osl-signflip (SungJun Cho), the file
mapping of the EEG-fMRI preprocessing from osl-pathfinder (Jize Zhang), and
the source reconstruction, parcellation and QC report share their code with
osl-dynamics. The SPM M/EEG reader was compiled from scripts by Evan Roberts
and Mark Hymers.
